    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "Summary of the Right to Information Act, 2005 (RTI Act, 2005)\nKey Provisions\n1.\tRight to Information\n•\tAll citizens have the right to information, subject to the Act's provisions.\n2.\tObligations of Public Authorities\n•\tMaintain, computerize, and network records for easy access.\n•\tPublish various details about the authority.\n•\tProvide reasons for administrative or quasi-judicial decisions.\n•\tSuo motu disclosure of information.\n3.\tDesignation of Public Information Officers\n•\tDesignate Central/State Public Information Officers and Assistants.\n4.\tExemptions and Penalties\n•\tExemptions: For certain organisations with exceptions.\n•\tPenalties: Include fines and imprisonment for non-compliance or misconduct.\n5.\tInformation Commissions\n•\tEstablishment of Central and State Information Commissions.\n6.\tMiscellaneous\n•\tProtection of Action in Good Faith\n•\tOverriding Effect\n•\tBar on Court Jurisdiction\n•\tMonitoring and Reporting",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
